@startuml
title The cookie game — one round at a time
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  ParticipantBorderColor #7A5BB5
  ArrowColor #7A5BB5
  LifeLineBorderColor #7A5BB5
  NoteBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  NoteBorderColor #7A5BB5
}

participant "Baker\n(the prover)" as B
participant "You\n(the verifier)" as Y

note over Y: the baker claims\nall the cookies score 6144 in total

B -> Y : left pile scores 2500, right pile scores 3644
note right of Y : 2500 + 3644 = 6144, so far so good
Y -> B : my random number is 3.7

B -> Y : the totals for the next split
note right of Y : they must add up\nto the answer at 3.7
Y -> B : my next random number is 0.5

... a few more rounds, one per direction of the grid ...

B -> Y : the score of one single cookie
note over Y #F3EEFB
  you walk over and taste that one cookie
  it matches: the whole total was honest
end note
@enduml
